BT /F1 9 Tf 40 800 Td 12 TL (General Conditions of Contract \(continued\)) ' () ' (101. The Contractor shall comply with all applicable laws, statutory rules and regulations in force,) ' (including the Indian Electricity Rules and the Central Electricity Authority \(Measures relating to Safety) ' (and Electric Supply\) Regulations.) ' () ' (102. All materials shall be new, of the best quality, and shall conform to the latest relevant Indian) ' (Standard Specifications, with BIS marking wherever applicable.) ' () ' (103. The Engineer-in-Charge shall have full powers to reject any material or work that does not conform) ' (to the specifications, and the Contractor shall remove such material from site at his own cost.) ' () ' (104. Payment shall be made within 30 days of receipt of the bill duly certified by the) ' (Engineer-in-Charge, subject to deduction of statutory taxes at source.) ' () ' (105. The defect liability period shall be twelve months from the date of completion. Any defect noticed) ' (during this period shall be rectified by the Contractor free of cost.) ' () ' (106. Liquidated damages at the rate of 0.5% of the contract value per week of delay, subject to a maximum) ' (of 10%, shall be levied for delay attributable to the Contractor.) ' () ' (107. The Contractor shall provide all tools, tackles, testing instruments and skilled manpower required) ' (for installation, testing and commissioning.) ' () ' (108. Insulation resistance, earth resistance and continuity tests shall be carried out in the presence of) ' (the Engineer-in-Charge and results recorded.) ' () ' (109. The Contractor shall maintain a site order book and comply with instructions recorded therein within) ' (the time specified.) ' () ' ET BT /F1 8 Tf 280 25 Td (Page 87 of 150) Tj ET
endstream
